course: dictionary
lesson: 12621
title: Knocking things loose
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To dislodge something is to knock, push or force it out of the place where it was stuck or fixed. «The strong wind dislodged a ripe apple from the branch.» The apple was held fast to the tree, and the wind moved it out of its place.
explain: Dislodge can also mean making a person leave a place or position, often by force. «The soldiers tried to dislodge the enemy from the hill.» The enemy did not want to leave, so the soldiers had to force them to go.
explain: Look at the words around dislodge for clues. Words like stuck, fixed, force or push show that something is being moved out of its place. Then try your meaning in the sentence: if «knocked out of its place» still makes sense, you have found it.
fact: «Dislodge» means to knock, push or force something out of a place where it was stuck or fixed.
fact: «Dislodge» can also mean to force a person out of a position or place.
fact: «Dislodge» is a verb: dislodge, dislodges, dislodged, dislodging.
fact: In first aid lessons, back blows can dislodge food that is stuck in someone's throat.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «The wind dislodged a ripe apple from the branch.» What does dislodged mean? | *Knocked or pushed out of its place | Painted bright red | Eaten very slowly | Tied tightly to the tree
exercise: «The soldiers tried to dislodge the enemy from the hill.» What does dislodge mean here? | Build a tall tower on the hill | Count how many there are | Invite them to a picnic | *Force them to leave their place
exercise: Ella tapped her shoe to dislodge the pebble. What does dislodge mean here? | Make the shoe bigger | Tie the shoe laces | *Shake or knock the pebble out of place | Put the pebble in a box
test: «The river was so strong it dislodged a large rock from the bank.» What does dislodged mean? | *Pushed out of its place | Painted | Frozen solid | Carefully counted
test: Which word means nearly the same as dislodge in «force the leader out of power»? | *Remove | Praise | Elect | Admire
exam: The flood began to dislodge the big boulder from the hillside. What does dislodge mean? | Paint in bright colours | *Knock out of its place | Turn into ice | Count slowly
